From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: unexport kbuild's recursive size helpers

The top-level Makefile exports every variable with a bare `export`.
GNU Make 4.4 passes exported variables to $(shell ...) invocations, so
that bare export makes make also export kbuild's size_append helper and
the cmd_* templates that call it. size_append expands to a $(shell ...)
command, so exporting it re-enters the shell function and make aborts
while building the module against a 4.4.94 kernel:

  scripts/Makefile.lib:382: *** prerequisites cannot be defined in recipes.  Stop.

Those kbuild command templates are internal and never need to be
exported. Unexport them right after the bare export.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 
 export WIFI_PROJ_DIR=$(PWD)
 export
+unexport size_append cmd_gzip cmd_bzip2 cmd_lzma cmd_lzo cmd_lz4 cmd_xzkern cmd_xzmisc
 -include $(src)/Makefile.build.kernel
 
 export DRIVER_PATH ?= $(PWD)
